      "id": 13034,
      "name": "Markqueue",
      "username": "Markqueue",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/a88e57/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-19T22:18:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hey guys,</p><p>Today I have been playing Legacy, Tempest, and Wraith against Plague Rat in Pike's Industrial Complex on iOS.</p><p>i was playing on my 2nd generation iPad (from 2010?), so granted it's not state of the art now in 2015, but I was noticing some major slowdowns in the game. &nbsp;And yes, I have played this configuration many times over, and I keep seeing the same slowdown occur.</p><p>When the environment is full of vats, Wraith has 2-3 Megacomputers out, and ... This seems to be the key, Tempest has Shielding Winds out.</p><p>i can wait up to fifteen minutes for a single update to an attack from the rat onto Tempest. &nbsp;I think one time it took an hour for all the vats and rats to attack just 1 round! &nbsp;It's almost unplayable.</p><p>Well, I figured it might be just be my hardware. &nbsp;So I today went out and bought a state of the art IPad Air 2. &nbsp;This is the fastest iPad Apple currently sells. &nbsp;This is probably on the order of 4-10x faster than my old iPad.</p><p>The new hardware does run faster, but once vats and rats and shielding winds come out, the game slows to a crawl. &nbsp;In fact, I am composing this message on my old iPad while I am running on the new hardware just waiting for the environment to finish its turn. &nbsp;It still hasn't.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Let me be clear.., I love this game! &nbsp;So much that I was willing to fork out the bucks for a new iPad so I could avoid the slowdown. &nbsp;It's slightly better, but it's still unplayable! &nbsp;It is currently taken 10? 15? Minutes for the environment to play and it's still not done!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>if I were to guess, it feels like some n^2 algorithm for iterating through the cards that may affect the environment. (Are you trying all combinations? &nbsp;Is it computing symbolically?) &nbsp;The worst offender seems to be shielding winds: it goes from slow updates to unplayably slow updates.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please please please fix this. &nbsp;It is unplayable in this configuration (and shielding winds is important to surviving the environment, esp. When the vat comes out that destroys all other vats)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Am I the only one seeing this?</p><p>&nbsp;Thanks for letting me vent.</p><p>i really do love the game and want it fixed so I can continue playing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
